  "notes": "{見|み}せつける is a transitive ichidan verb. It combines {見|み}せる (to show) with つける (to attach/force), creating the nuance of deliberately displaying or flaunting.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{見|み}せつけている indicates an ongoing display or show of force.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- XをYに{見|み}せつける (flaunt X to Y)\n- Xを{見|み}せつける (show off X)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {実力|じつりょく}を{見|み}せつける (show off one's ability)\n- {力|ちから}の{差|さ}を{見|み}せつける (demonstrate the gap in strength)\n- {存在感|そんざいかん}を{見|み}せつける (make one's presence felt)\n\nThe word often carries a competitive or confrontational nuance, implying that the display is intended to intimidate, impress, or provoke envy.",
